The src folder contains all the source code for the React application, serving as the core directory where the main App component, TypeScript definitions, and application initialization logic are stored. It houses the essential files that define the application's structure and functionality, with main.tsx bootstrapping the React rendering process and App.tsx acting as the primary component that orchestrates the user interface. This folder represents the heart of the project where all the development work takes place, containing everything needed to build and run the web client application.
